    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Axe Ghost</strong> is an unforgiving turn-based spatial battle against an advancing monster horde. You play cards to manipulate enemies. Group them up and wipe them out to climb the daily leaderboard.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2712670/extras/d194ed1d67870f7067dc5f1588957ab6.poster.avif?t=1749318120\" width=616 height=253 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2712670/extras/d194ed1d67870f7067dc5f1588957ab6.webm?t=1749318120\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each run lasts around 20 minutes. The weapons dealt let you push, swap, clone, slice, freeze, magnetize and destroy the advancing monsters before they reach the bottom of the grid. Group them cleverly - the more monsters you destroy in a single attack, the more each one is worth. Accept optional constraints in the form of <strong>Quests</strong> to multiply your score. Spend <strong>Coins</strong> to play extra cards in critical moments.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2712670/extras/a992cc183814c5655062380bf588ecc8.poster.avif?t=1749318120\" width=616 height=253 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2712670/extras/a992cc183814c5655062380bf588ecc8.webm?t=1749318120\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Lord Garnemar</strong>, the loathsome boss, is only vulnerable when surrounded on four sides by the same type of monster. Defeat him before deadly robots overrun the battlefield and the timer runs out.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2712670/extras/3ef3feb51aff13c3b11229f9bdffafc5.poster.avif?t=1749318120\" width=616 height=300 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2712670/extras/3ef3feb51aff13c3b11229f9bdffafc5.webm?t=1749318120\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2712670/extras/3ef3feb51aff13c3b11229f9bdffafc5.mp4?t=1749318120\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I hear them approaching.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Axe Ghost</strong> is an unforgiving turn-based spatial battle against an advancing monster horde. You play cards to manipulate enemies. Group them up and wipe them out to climb the daily leaderboard.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2712670/extras/d194ed1d67870f7067dc5f1588957ab6.poster.avif?t=1749318120\" width=616 height=253 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2712670/extras/d194ed1d67870f7067dc5f1588957ab6.webm?t=1749318120\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each run lasts around 20 minutes. The weapons dealt let you push, swap, clone, slice, freeze, magnetize and destroy the advancing monsters before they reach the bottom of the grid. Group them cleverly - the more monsters you destroy in a single attack, the more each one is worth. Accept optional constraints in the form of <strong>Quests</strong> to multiply your score. Spend <strong>Coins</strong> to play extra cards in critical moments.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2712670/extras/a992cc183814c5655062380bf588ecc8.poster.avif?t=1749318120\" width=616 height=253 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2712670/extras/a992cc183814c5655062380bf588ecc8.webm?t=1749318120\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Lord Garnemar</strong>, the loathsome boss, is only vulnerable when surrounded on four sides by the same type of monster. Defeat him before deadly robots overrun the battlefield and the timer runs out.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2712670/extras/3ef3feb51aff13c3b11229f9bdffafc5.poster.avif?t=1749318120\" width=616 height=300 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2712670/extras/3ef3feb51aff13c3b11229f9bdffafc5.webm?t=1749318120\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2712670/extras/3ef3feb51aff13c3b11229f9bdffafc5.mp4?t=1749318120\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I hear them approaching.</p>",
    "short_description": "In Axe Ghost you cleverly push monsters around a grid and blow them up in turn-based spatial combat. Take on the Daily Challenge and face off against the loathsome Garnemar!",
    "supported_languages": "English, German, Simplified Chinese, Korean, Traditional Chinese",
    "reviews": "\u201cWhat I like most about Axe Ghost is how it takes some game things that feel quite ancient and primitive and turns them into a random conundrum generator, offering meaty, puzzly turns that sometimes had me stumped for good stretches.\u201d<br>Rock Paper Shotgun<br><br>\u201cAXE GHOST is just that unique of an experience. I even have trouble trying to ascribe a genre to it.\u201d<br>MASTERPIECE! \u2013 Tiny Gaming<br>",
